    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 3/3), and the full test suite consists of exactly that one acceptance class plus helpers.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the optional, region-validated `postcode` field end-to-end, following the app's existing Spring conventions:\n\n**Contract / DTO** \u2014 `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`: added an optional `postcode` property to the `OwnerFields` schema (`pattern: \"^[0-9]{4}$\"`, **not** in `required`). Since `Owner` is `allOf` `OwnerFields`, this generates the field on both the request DTO and the response DTO, and Bean Validation rejects any non-4-digit value with 400 (this is what rejects the malformed `\"12\"`).\n\n**Entity** \u2014 `Owner.java`: added the `postcode` field with `@Column(name=\"postcode\")`, a `@Pattern` guard, getter/setter, and a `toString` entry. MapStruct maps it automatically by name, so store-and-return works with no mapper change.\n\n**Region rule** \u2014 `mapper/Region.java`: attached each region's inclusive postcode range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) to the existing city\u2192region enum and added `acceptsPostcode(int)`, keeping the region-scoped facts in their single documented home.\n\n**Validation wiring** \u2014 added `InvalidPostcodeException` and a matching 400 handler in `ExceptionControllerAdvice` (mirroring the telephone handler, reporting the `postcode` field). `OwnerRestControllerV1` now calls a new `validatePostcode(...)` in both `normalizeAndValidate` (create) and `updateOwner`: when a postcode is present and the city maps to a known region, an out-of-range value is rejected with 400; an unknown-region city accepts any 4-digit postcode; absent postcode is skipped entirely (backward-compatible). Update also persists the postcode.\n\n**Schema** \u2014 added the `postcode` column to all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres).\n\nThe three checkpoints \u2014 valid postcode stored & returned, owner accepted without a postcode, and malformed postcode rejected with 400 \u2014 all pass, and the region out-of-range case is handled per spec even though it isn't directly asserted by a test.",
